                <pb facs="0699" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg685"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton, Secretary of State, to Mr. Hall, district
                        attorney</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Confidential.—Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1849-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 7, 1849</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Prescott Hall</hi>,
                        Esq.,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States District Attorney, New
                        York:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Act according to your own discretion in the
                    case of * * *; and the vessels also. Break up the enterprise—that is the great
                    object. If <pb facs="0700" n="686" xml:id="pg686"/> the Government had no other
                    motive, it is all-important to save the lives of the ignorant dupes of the
                    project. Their fate in Cuba would be most disastrous. No vindictive proceedings
                    are desirable, in my judgment, after the enterprise is broken up. * * *</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. M. CLAYTON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
